{title: You Are Good}
{song_number: 31}
{language: en}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G]I want to scream it out from every mountain top:
Your [C]goodness knows no bounds, Your goodness never stops.
Your [Em]mercy follows me, Your kindness fills my life;
[G]Your love amazes [D]me!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And I [G]sing because You are good, and I
dance because You are good, and I [C]shout because
You are good. You are good to [G]me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G]Nothing and no one comes anywhere close to You.
The [C]earth and oceans deep only reflect this truth.
And in my [Em]darkest night You shine as bright as day;
[G]Your love amazes [D]me!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And I [G]sing because You are good, and I
dance because You are good, and I [C]shout because
You are good. You are good to [G]me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
With a [Am7]cry of praise, [C]my heart will proclaim:
You are [G]good, You are [Bm]good!
In the [Am7]sun or rain, [C]my life celebrates:
You are [G]good, You are [D]good!
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
And I [G]sing because You are good, and I
dance because You are good, and I [C]shout because
You are good. You are good to [G]me.
{end_of_chorus}
